#!/usr/bin/env beg

Accept a source directory and a new destination directory.
Copy the tree, lowercasing names and replacing runs of spaces and underscores
with one hyphen in each filename and directory name.

Update relative Markdown links and images, including reference definitions,
to point to their corresponding renamed files or directories in the copy.
Keep link text, fragments, and queries. Leave external links, links outside the
tree, and the original files alone.

If any paths collide after renaming, list the collisions on stderr and exit
before creating the destination. On success, print the destination path.
